---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<astro:head>
	<title>Edge City Fellowship Application</title>
	<meta name="description" content="Application responses for the Edge City popup village fellowship." />
</astro:head>

<Layout>
	<main id="edge-app">
		<section class="container">
			<h1>Edge City Fellowship Application</h1>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Why do you want to join an Edge City popup village?</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p>I have an unwavering commitment to surrounding myself with people who inspire me. Over the past three years, I've dropped out of a top 5 computer science undergrad (Illinois), helped scaled an education startup to 1M users, and moved to San Frascisco, all in the name of pursuing the development of more humane technology. Being at Edge Patagonia feels like a natural extension of this journey.</p>
					<p>I spent this last summer at the Nautilus residency, where I focused on making art and studying scientific history, especially Cybernetics. Now, I've decided to come back to my ML research roots and start a company : )</p>
					<p>The problem is: I'm not sure what my company is about. I hope to nail this down at Edge. I've become evermore interested in vasocomputation after attending Mike Johnson's talk about the consciousness residency at Edge. I have studied buddhism and practiced meditation by myself for the past three years, but had never though there were groups of people systematically studying these more qualitative aspects of brain experience through the lens of computer science.</p>
					<p>I have formal training in phylosophy of computer science (and CS itself!!) and have worked extensively in software. I was thinking of joining a top research lab (was talking to anthropic, prime intellect), but decided to give myself these next two months to study more on Qualia in order to see if there's an opportunity for me to be useful in this space.</p>
					<p>As a last tidbit: I am a semi-professional bossa nova and jazz guitar player. I play at bars, small events, and have dedicated the last six years of my life to this craft that keeps me close to Brazil.</p>
					<p>I hope that, by being at Edge, I can bring my experience in edTech, latin american music, software, and my enthusiasm about consciousness research together. I'm certain I'll find ways to be useful to the scientific community, as well to Edge's community at large.</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Describe a project you have designed/led or initiative you have undertaken that demonstrates your commitment to building and creating positive change. Feel free to add links.</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p>When I was 18, I joined the founding team of Teachy, a Brazilian edtech startup focused on helping high school teachers in developing countries. In Brazil, like many other places, teachers are severely overworked and underpaid. Most have to prepare dozens of classes each week with little time or support. We built tools that could help teachers prepare lesson plans and adapt content, so they could spend less time preparing and more time teaching.</p>
					<p>I led our machine learning work. I set up the first data pipelines and trained models to turn raw curriculum into structured lessons, which quickly became the core of our product. As the company grew from 4 people to over 30, I had to figure out how to own technical efforts and train peers while being the youngest person there. I had particular difficulty admitting when I was unable to get things done in time. It took months of failing and a lot of personal introspection. I do think I became a better leader in those two years.</p>
					<p>Most importantly, I remember when we got our first message from a high school teacher in Brazil: "Thank you, I now have time to spend the weekend with my kids."</p>
					<p>By the time I left, Teachy had reached more than 2 million teachers and raised a Series A. Leaving was a super hard decision, but I stayed three extra months to make sure the round was done well and the team was taken care of. I left tired and beaten, but super grateful to have done something I genuinely think was good for my people.</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Tell us about a community / city / group that is meaningful to you.</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p>Nautilus is a three month residency program for young polymaths. It is a temporary home, in the heart of San Francisco, for kids aged 17 to 22 who want to drop everything else behind and work exclusively on their crafts. I was fortunate enough to be one of eleven selected for the first cohort of this program.</p>
					<p>Nautilus is dear to me because it helped me find a footing after a rough period of my journey, and it was where I had the unique chance to help people like me find a footing as well.</p>
					<p>I dropped out of college to pursue Teachy, and though we had two years of amazing growth, I was leaving the company on a low. Along with losing equity, I lost a sense of purpose. My biggest fear was ending up back in my hometown with no degree, no success story and no way to ever go back to doing high-impact work abroad. I feared I had "lost my chance" to do great work.</p>
					<p>Funnily enough, Zelda's biggest advice to me was "I have no expectation for you or any of the protegés". There was something so immensely freeing that came with not being expected to perform. I could talk in depth about the work I developed at Nautilus. I did metal art, played music on the street, organized a symposium on cybernetics, and wrote software for archiving blogs. But most important than my work, I love Nautilus because I got to meet friends who have had the same struggles, who also came from seemingly nowhere, and who have also feared never being discovered again.</p>
					<p>I lived ninety days with Zebo, Neel, Lena, Sommaiya and others. Through the letters we exchanged last week, I feel so fortunate to have met them: to have helped and to have been helped. My fear is now gone. I'm pursuing an O-1 Visa in the US and starting a company. I'm excited for the future again, thanks to them.</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>What are 1-3 things you need right now that could greatly accelerate your journey / impact?</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<ul>
						<li>Mentorship on how to navigate my interests, to think strategically about my carrer (ML Research, Bossa Nova jazz)</li>
						<li>Opportunities in top research spaces in AI / Consciousness (Emmet Shear-aligned)</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Optional: links or documents that elaborate on the above</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p><a href="https://falso.net">https://falso.net</a> &lt;-- documentation on my work</p>
					<p><a href="https://falso.net">https://falso.net/sfcs</a> &lt;-- cybernetics symposium : )</p>
					<p><a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bnecw8japSRJoI975p58rMXcP9AeARZQ/view?usp=sharing">Resume (Google Drive)</a></p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Have you been referred by anyone from the Edge City community?</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p>Zelda Poem, <a href="mailto:zeldapoem@gmail.com">zeldapoem@gmail.com</a>, +33 652051325. She runs Nautilus, the fellowship house I am living in right now. She is also a friend.</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="qa">
				<summary>Is there anything else you would like us to know?</summary>
				<div class="answer">
					<p>My greatest strength is being caring, kind and present to the communities I'm a part of. (Un)fortunately this cannot be measured in KPI's, but I truly believe it is my greatest strength. It's what kept my last company afloat at times, and hopefuly it helped Nautilus be a better community as well.</p>
				</div>
			</details>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	#edge-app {
		min-height: 100vh;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.container {
		max-width: 820px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 28px 20px 64px 20px;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0 0 8px 0;
		font-size: 28px;
	}

	.note {
		opacity: 0.75;
		margin-bottom: 20px;
	}

	.qa {
		border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
		padding: 12px 14px;
		border-radius: 6px;
		margin: 12px 0;
		background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02);
	}

	.qa > summary {
		cursor: pointer;
		font-weight: 700;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.qa[open] > summary {
		margin-bottom: 10px;
	}

	.answer p {
		margin: 0 0 12px 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; }
</style>


